Description:
Hi all, we have recently added a 'Partner Mode' to our Clari and I am trying to build out the columns queries. Although I am using the same queries as the current active tabs (AE, RM Expansion) I am not seeing the correct data come into the partner tab. I have 2 initial questions but would be grateful for some support in building this correctly;

1. I am using the SFDC field 'Partner Sale Type' to include actuals for 2 items on this drop list on the field however it will not let me add it as the following; 'Partner Sale Type' is "Sourced by the partner, Assisted by the Partner" it will only let me add it as the following 'Partner Sale Type' is "Sourced by the partner" AND 'Partner Sale Type' is "Assisted by the partner" AND 'Partner Sale Subtype' is not "Intercom-Funded Service partner Assist". I don't see an option in the field configuration tab to group this picklist.

2. Although I am using the same parameters as the AE and RM queries for the various columns I'mnot getting the expec

o: 2443 has experienced performance issues that look to be related to the usage of NOT statements on string fields throughout the template.

Can the team work with the customer to rework the formulas used in forecasting to no longer use NOT statements with string fields?

An example of a NOT statement using a string field is below:
{
                  "type": "EXPRESSION",
                  "operator": "NOT",
                  "operands": [
                    {
                      "type": "FIELD",
                      "id": "opportunity.deal_type__c",
                      "value": "Monthly"
                    }
                  ]
                }

Change the quota name for the following tabs:-
dx_specialist_quota_monthly_aep_arravg to dx_specialist_quota_aep_arravg_monthly;
dx_sam_quota_monthly_arravg to dx_sam_quota_arravg_monthly;
dx_specialist_quota_arravg to dx_specialist_quota_monthly_arravg_monthly;

Request to expedite this request as i need to perform quota upload functions
